WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.500
Welcome to OpsCrew, an autonomous multi-agent copilot
built in Google AI Studio Build for the AI Builder Cup 2026.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:20.000
Deployed on Google Cloud Run with dual-mode Vertex AI & Gemini API, Firestore, and Secret Manager.
Now, let us examine OpsCrew operating live in production.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:34.796
I explicitly start a Firebase visitor session. Synthetic example DEV-04 is a
$38 parking expense for employee SYNTH-EMP-100, with a missing receipt.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:51.495
Gemini extracts facts, then a separately prompted Planner proposes handling steps.
A Reviewer checks the proposal. This timer measures elapsed time.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:06.053
Completed role attempts appear after the response; it is not live progress inside each stage.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:17.753
The result requests receipt evidence. Clause SYN-004 asks for an itemized receipt or explanation.
The passing plan and review grant no permission to create a case, reimburse or pay.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:36.680
I prepare human confirmation, inspect this specific plan, and explicitly authorize the record.
The checkbox starts unchecked. I now submit that authorization.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:48.507
Success appears only after a separate read of the saved record from Firestore.
The case record is atomic and policy-verified.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:58.300
I refresh visitor history and reopen the same case to verify state parity.
OpsCrew requires human authorization and never issues payment automatically.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:11.520
Thank you for watching! Explore OpsCrew live on Google Cloud Run.
Autonomous multi-agent copilot built for the AI Builder Cup 2026.
